264
00:18:22,299 --> 00:18:25,299
After the particle diameter is reduced, it can be reduced to 1.

265
00:18:25,299 --> 00:18:32,299
You can see the effect between the plates when there is a different conflict thickness in the picture.

266
00:18:32,299 --> 00:18:38,299
The surface diameter of the model refers to the layer between the plate and the model.

267
00:18:38,299 --> 00:18:41,299
And the safety distance set on the model surface.

268
00:18:41,299 --> 00:18:45,299
Its default value is 3 mm.

269
00:18:45,299 --> 00:18:51,299
Reducing the surface diameter of the model will also make the clothing closer to the model.

270
00:18:55,299 --> 00:18:58,299
Next is the quality of the simulation.

271
00:18:58,299 --> 00:19:02,299
Here you can choose the normal speed or the test wear speed.

272
00:19:04,299 --> 00:19:07,299
The normal speed of the simulation will be faster.

273
00:19:08,299 --> 00:19:12,299
It is better to balance the simulation speed and accuracy.

274
00:19:12,299 --> 00:19:16,299
The test wear simulation is a more accurate physical characteristic of the simulation fabric.

275
00:19:16,299 --> 00:19:19,299
In order to get a more accurate clothing effect.

276
00:19:19,299 --> 00:19:21,299
The speed will be slower.

277
00:19:21,299 --> 00:19:24,299
Usually when checking the test body, use the simulation mode.

278
00:19:24,299 --> 00:19:28,299
